<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johannes van Walbeeck</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johannes van Walbeeck was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> navigator and commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-west-india-company">Dutch West India Company</a>. In 1634 he led the expedition that captured Curaçao from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, giving the company a naval base, salt pans and a foothold close to the Spanish Main. He became the island's first Dutch governor, and Aruba and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonaire">Bonaire</a> were taken soon afterwards.</p></div>
